---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Resizer from '../components/Resizer.astro';
import SEOContentResize from '../components/SEOContentResize.astro';

const SEO_TITLE = "Create Passport Size Photo Online — Instant Cropper";
const SEO_DESC = "Convert your photos to exact passport size dimensions instantly. Perfect for US passport (600x600 px) or visa applications. 100% private.";

const uniqueTitle = "Comprehensive Guide: Creating the Perfect Passport Size Photo Online";

const uniqueContent = `
  <p class="seo-p">
    Applying for an official document can be stressful, and dealing with photo rejections is the last thing you need. Whether you are submitting a <strong>passport renewal</strong>, a <strong>visa application</strong>, applying for an <strong>Aadhaar card</strong> update, or submitting forms for <strong>college admissions</strong> and competitive exams (like UPSC, SSC, NEET, or IBPS), having the correct <strong>passport size photo dimensions</strong> is absolutely critical.
  </p>
  <p class="seo-p">
    Our <strong>passport size photo maker online</strong> allows you to instantly crop and resize any standard picture into a professionally formatted official photo. The tool operates 100% locally in your browser, meaning your sensitive identity photos are never uploaded to our servers, keeping your data entirely private.
  </p>

  <h3 class="seo-h3">Passport Photo Size in India vs. Other Countries</h3>
  <p class="seo-p">
    Passport dimensions vary heavily depending on the issuing country. Uploading a US-sized photo to an Indian portal will likely result in an automatic rejection. Here are the exact specifications:
  </p>
  <ul class="seo-list" style="margin-bottom: 32px; list-style: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
    <li><strong style="color: var(--color-ink);">Indian Passport Size:</strong> The standard <strong>passport photo size in India</strong> is <strong>2x2 inches</strong> (51 x 51 mm). In pixel terms, for a 300 DPI upload, this translates to exactly <strong>600x600 pixels</strong>.</li>
    <li><strong style="color: var(--color-ink);">Indian Stamp Size (for Pan Card/Exams):</strong> Often required for specific domestic forms, the size is 3.5 cm x 4.5 cm (approx 413x531 pixels at 300 DPI).</li>
    <li><strong style="color: var(--color-ink);">US Passport & Visa:</strong> The US standard is also 2x2 inches (51 x 51 mm) or 600x600 pixels.</li>
    <li><strong style="color: var(--color-ink);">UK & Europe Passport:</strong> The standard size is usually 35 mm wide by 45 mm high.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3 class="seo-h3">Strict Photo Requirements You Must Follow</h3>
  <p class="seo-p">
    Achieving the right pixel dimensions is only the first step. To ensure your photo is accepted by automated government AI and human reviewers, you must adhere to these global standards:
  </p>
  <div class="seo-steps" style="margin-bottom: 40px;">
    <ol class="seo-list">
      <li>
        <div class="seo-step-num">01</div>
        <div>
          <h4 class="seo-step-title">White Background</h4>
          <p class="seo-p-small">Your photo must have a plain white or off-white background. No textures, patterns, or shadows should be visible behind your head.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <div class="seo-step-num">02</div>
        <div>
          <h4 class="seo-step-title">70-80% Face Coverage</h4>
          <p class="seo-p-small">Your head must be centered and take up roughly 70% to 80% of the total frame. Ensure your full face is visible from the top of your hair to the bottom of your chin.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <div class="seo-step-num">03</div>
        <div>
          <h4 class="seo-step-title">No Glasses Rule</h4>
          <p class="seo-p-small">Starting recently, countries like the US and India explicitly prohibit wearing eyeglasses in passport photos. Even if you wear prescription glasses daily, you must remove them to avoid glare and frame obstruction.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <div class="seo-step-num">04</div>
        <div>
          <h4 class="seo-step-title">Neutral Expression</h4>
          <p class="seo-p-small">Maintain a neutral facial expression with both eyes open and your mouth closed. Avoid smiling widely or frowning.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <h3 class="seo-h3">Common Rejection Reasons & How to Avoid Them</h3>
  <p class="seo-p">
    Automated portals will instantly reject your photo if it falls short of the requirements. The most frequent causes of rejection include:
  </p>
  <ul class="seo-list" style="margin-bottom: 32px; list-style: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
    <li><strong style="color: var(--color-ink);">Incorrect Aspect Ratio:</strong> Uploading a rectangular photo when a square 600x600 px is required. Use our crop tool to lock in the 1:1 ratio.</li>
    <li><strong style="color: var(--color-ink);">Poor Lighting:</strong> Harsh shadows across the face or background. Take your photo facing a natural light source (like a window).</li>
    <li><strong style="color: var(--color-ink);">Blurry or Pixelated:</strong> Taking a photo from too far away and zooming in. Keep the camera at eye level, roughly 4-5 feet away.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3 class="seo-h3">Step-by-Step Guide: Using Our Passport Photo Maker</h3>
  <p class="seo-p">
    Ready to create your perfect ID photo? Follow these simple steps using the tool above:
  </p>
  <p class="seo-p">
    <strong>Step 1:</strong> Click the upload box and select your raw image.<br/>
    <strong>Step 2:</strong> Use the width and height inputs to set your exact required dimensions. For US and Indian passports, it defaults to <strong>600x600 pixels</strong>.<br/>
    <strong>Step 3:</strong> Adjust the cropping box. Ensure your face is centered and covers about 70-80% of the box area.<br/>
    <strong>Step 4:</strong> Click "Download". Your perfectly sized image is saved locally to your device, ready for immediate upload to the official portal.
  </p>
`;

const customFaqs = [
  {
    q: "What is the exact passport size photo dimension for an Indian passport?",
    a: "The official dimension for an Indian passport is 2 x 2 inches (51 mm x 51 mm). When uploading online, this translates to exactly 600x600 pixels at 300 DPI. Our tool defaults to these exact measurements."
  },
  {
    q: "Can I wear glasses in my passport photo?",
    a: "No. Under the latest strict guidelines for most countries, including India and the USA, you are not permitted to wear glasses in your passport photo. You must remove them to prevent lens glare and frame obstruction."
  },
  {
    q: "Will this tool work for UPSC, SSC, or Aadhaar card portals?",
    a: "Yes! While standard passports require 600x600 pixels, many Indian exams like UPSC, SSC, NEET, or Aadhaar updates require sizes like 3.5cm x 4.5cm. You can manually enter the exact pixel width and height (e.g., 413x531 pixels) into our tool to create a compliant photo."
  },
  {
    q: "Is it safe to upload my face to this passport size photo maker online?",
    a: "Absolutely. Our engine processes the image locally within your browser. Your sensitive identity photo is never sent to our servers, ensuring 100% privacy and protection from data leaks."
  },
  {
    q: "Why was my photo rejected for 'face size not matching'?",
    a: "This happens when your head is either too zoomed in or too far away. Your head (from the top of the hair to the bottom of the chin) must take up 70% to 80% of the total photo height. Use our crop tool to precisely box your face before downloading."
  }
];
---

<Layout title={SEO_TITLE} description={SEO_DESC}>
  <style is:global>
    :root {
      /* Warm Orange Theme */
      --color-lime: #ff7e33;
    }
  </style>

  <section class="relative z-20 pt-20 container-stripe">
    <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 48px;">
      <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; background: rgba(255, 126, 51, 0.08); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 126, 51, 0.2); border-radius: 100px; padding: 5px 14px; margin-bottom: 24px;">
        <span style="font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.6875rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em; color: var(--color-lime);">Feature: Passport Cropper</span>
      </div>

      <h1 style="font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 8vw, 4.5rem); line-height: 1; margin: 0 0 24px; letter-spacing: -0.05em;">
        Passport Size <br/>
        <span style="color: var(--color-lime);">Photo Maker.</span>
      </h1>
      <p style="color: var(--color-ink-2); font-size: 1.125rem; margin-bottom: 24px; max-width: 500px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; line-height: 1.6;">
        Instantly resize and crop your photos to meet official passport and visa requirements. Pre-set to US Standard 600x600 pixels.
      </p>
    </div>

    <Resizer allowMultiple={false} defaultWidth={600} defaultHeight={600} />
  </section>

  <SEOContentResize 
    isPassport={true} 
    customTitle={uniqueTitle}
    uniqueContent={uniqueContent}
    customFaqs={customFaqs}
  />
</Layout>
